# Cloudflare Pages routing.
# / (index.html)        = public marketing page. It forwards any auth-callback
#                         hash/query (magic links, invites, ?join=) to /portal/.
# /portal/ (index.html) = the portal app (login + client/team dashboards).
#
# The portal MUST live at a directory index (portal/index.html), NOT a bare
# portal.html: Pages route-normalizes "/portal.html" to "/portal" with a 308,
# and "/portal" then falls into the /* rewrite whose .html target 308s again —
# an infinite redirect loop (Safari: "too many redirects"). Directory indexes
# are served directly with no extension redirect, exactly like the site root.
#
# Order matters — first match wins. The explicit /portal.html rule catches any
# old links (e.g. already-sent emails) from the brief window that URL existed.
/portal.html    /portal/    301
/portal         /portal/    301
# Standalone legal/marketing pages. Explicit 200 rewrites BEFORE the SPA
# fallback so both the bare and trailing-slash forms serve the real page
# instead of being swallowed by /* into the portal app.
/privacy        /privacy/index.html    200
/privacy/       /privacy/index.html    200
/terms          /terms/index.html      200
/terms/         /terms/index.html      200
# SPA fallback: any path that is not a real static file serves the portal app
# (HTTP 200, no redirect) so client-side routes and magic-link callbacks
# resolve instead of 404ing.
/*    /portal/index.html    200
